 "case:briefing.0": "Larkspur House, Wiltshire. Sunday 18 November 1962, nine o’clock in the morning.",
 "case:briefing.1": "Last night Lionel Thorne — sixty-three, self-made, founder of Thorne Instruments — was found dead at his study desk, less than an hour before the midnight toast at which he meant to ‘clear the decks’ with an announcement.",
 "case:briefing.2": "The storm flooded the only bridge out of the valley. No one came and no one went. Six people were in the house with him.",
 "case:briefing.3": "Constable Pike, out of his depth and soaked to the knees, has sealed the study and asked you to look into it before the county men can get through. His notes are in the file. Everyone, he says, has something to hide.",
 "case:briefing.4": "Find out who killed Lionel Thorne, how it was done and why — and be ready to prove it.",
 "case:epilogue.0": "Eleanor Voss said nothing at all when Constable Pike took her arm. It was only at the county police station, faced with the time switch and the half-signed letter, that she began to talk — precisely, as she did everything.",
 "case:epilogue.1": "She had been taking money through Calder & Rowe for eight years: forty thousand pounds, typed into existence one invoice at a time. When Lionel ringed an invoice in red and booked the auditors for Monday, she knew she had one weekend.",
 "case:epilogue.2": "The rabbit powder at four o’clock. The letters, so that Lionel would be bent over his desk with his whisky at his elbow while she stood beside him. The 15 November reel, because Hobbs had never heard that dictation. And the time switch set for a quarter past ten, because everyone in the house knew Hobbs banked the study fire then — and that he would never interrupt the master’s dictation.",
 "case:epilogue.3": "She had planned for everything except Lionel Thorne dying halfway through his own name, on a letter she had put in front of him.",
 "case:epilogue.4": "Daniel Thorne went to work at Thorne Instruments in the spring — as a junior clerk. Gerald Finch sold his shares to Hartley. Margaret Thorne and Felix Harrow were married, very quietly, the following year.",
 "case:epilogue.5": "Hobbs still banks the study fire at a quarter past ten every night. He says the house doesn’t feel right otherwise.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse.levels.0": "Review your board. Who was in the study when Lionel died, who gained an alibi from the 10.15 ‘voice’, and who needed him silenced before Monday?",
 "case:hints.h_accuse.levels.1": "Every part of the accusation needs a card: opportunity, the false alibi and the motive. If one is missing, the hints above will have pointed you to it — re-read your notebook.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse.levels.2": "The killer is Eleanor Voss: cyanide in the whisky, to hide her embezzlement from Monday’s audit. Prove it with the half-signed letter or Finch’s sighting, the time switch, and the Calder & Rowe deduction (from the invoice on Lionel’s desk and Eleanor’s typewriter).",
 "case:hints.h_accuse_ready.levels.0": "You may already have enough to make an arrest. Who was in the study when Lionel died, and who gained an alibi from the 10.15 ‘voice’?",
 "case:hints.h_accuse_ready.levels.1": "Only one person sat at the bridge table at 10.15 and was also in the study between 9.25 and 10.00. Why would they need Lionel dead before Monday?",
 "case:hints.h_accuse_ready.levels.2": "Accuse Eleanor Voss: cyanide in the whisky, to hide her embezzlement from Monday’s audit. Prove it with the half-signed letter (or Finch’s sighting), the time switch (or your time-switch deduction), and the Calder & Rowe deduction.",
 "case:hints.h_affair.levels.0": "Margaret and Dr. Harrow tell the same story about the drawing room. Perhaps too neatly.",
 "case:hints.h_affair.levels.1": "Look through Margaret’s things in the drawing room — and visit the conservatory.",
 "case:hints.h_affair.levels.2": "Challenge Margaret’s and Harrow’s drawing-room statements with the note from the sewing basket, or the shawl and cigarette case.",
 "case:hints.h_calder.levels.0": "Lionel ringed one invoice in red. Why?",
 "case:hints.h_calder.levels.1": "Calder & Rowe’s invoices have a peculiar typeface. Have you seen it anywhere else in the house?",
 "case:hints.h_calder.levels.2": "Answer ‘A sham firm’ with the Calder & Rowe invoice and Eleanor’s typewriter.",
 "case:hints.h_daniel.levels.0": "Everyone suspects Daniel. But is his own account of the evening true?",
 "case:hints.h_daniel.levels.1": "Daniel says he never went near the study. Something in the study says otherwise.",
 "case:hints.h_daniel.levels.2": "Ask Daniel where he went after dinner, then challenge that statement with the burnt IOU or the bronze bookend.",
 "case:hints.h_daniel_cleared.levels.0": "Now that you know when Lionel died, look again at the obvious suspect.",
 "case:hints.h_daniel_cleared.levels.1": "Rosie’s statement says where Daniel was during the crucial half hour.",
 "case:hints.h_daniel_cleared.levels.2": "Answer ‘No — he was in the billiards room’ with Rosie Dunn’s statement and your time-of-death deduction.",
 "case:hints.h_eleanor_letters.levels.0": "Eleanor insists Lionel was well when she left him. Is there any trace of what happened while she was there?",
 "case:hints.h_eleanor_letters.levels.1": "Look closely at the letters she brought him that night. They’re in her office.",
 "case:hints.h_eleanor_letters.levels.2": "Challenge Eleanor’s ‘perfectly well when I left’ statement with the half-signed letter from her out-tray.",
 "case:hints.h_eleanor_typing.levels.0": "Eleanor says she spent the evening typing. Does anyone’s account disagree?",
 "case:hints.h_eleanor_typing.levels.1": "Re-read the housemaid’s statement in your case file — or look at Eleanor’s fireplace.",
 "case:hints.h_eleanor_typing.levels.2": "Challenge Eleanor’s ‘typing in my office’ statement with Rosie Dunn’s statement or the cold grate.",
 "case:hints.h_embezzle.levels.0": "Eleanor would have you believe Calder & Rowe is perfectly ordinary. You know better.",
 "case:hints.h_embezzle.levels.1": "Your deductions are cards too. You can present them in an interrogation.",
 "case:hints.h_embezzle.levels.2": "Ask Eleanor about Calder & Rowe, then challenge her answer with your ‘Calder & Rowe is a sham’ deduction.",
 "case:hints.h_finch.levels.0": "Gerald Finch’s quiet evening in the library is rather convenient.",
 "case:hints.h_finch.levels.1": "The telephone in the hall keeps more secrets than you might think.",
 "case:hints.h_finch.levels.2": "Examine the telephone pad in the Hall, then challenge Finch’s library statement with it.",
 "case:hints.h_finch_saw.levels.0": "Finch spent twenty minutes standing in the hall. What might he have seen?",
 "case:hints.h_finch_saw.levels.1": "The hall telephone has a view straight down the study corridor.",
 "case:hints.h_finch_saw.levels.2": "Ask Finch what he could see from the telephone.",
 "case:hints.h_harrow_blow.levels.0": "Dr. Harrow was very quick to name the cause of death.",
 "case:hints.h_harrow_blow.levels.1": "Something in the study smells wrong for a man who was simply struck down.",
 "case:hints.h_harrow_blow.levels.2": "Ask Dr. Harrow how Lionel died, then challenge his statement with the wilted fern.",
 "case:hints.h_hobbs.levels.0": "Servants often notice what the family misses.",
 "case:hints.h_hobbs.levels.1": "Hobbs was the last person to hear Lionel ‘alive’.",
 "case:hints.h_hobbs.levels.2": "Interrogate Hobbs and ask him about a quarter past ten.",
 "case:hints.h_knees.levels.0": "Whoever set the time switch had to remove it before morning. When could they have done it?",
 "case:hints.h_knees.levels.1": "In the confusion after the body was found, somebody may have noticed something.",
 "case:hints.h_knees.levels.2": "Ask Gerald Finch what he saw when everyone rushed into the study.",
 "case:hints.h_office.levels.0": "Lionel’s correspondence and dictation are kept somewhere you haven’t been yet.",
 "case:hints.h_office.levels.1": "Eleanor Voss holds the key to her office.",
 "case:hints.h_office.levels.2": "Ask Eleanor where she was after dinner — she’ll hand you the key.",
 "case:hints.h_papers.levels.0": "Lionel’s own papers may say more about his last week than any witness.",
 "case:hints.h_papers.levels.1": "Look through what’s on Lionel’s desk: his diary, and the invoices he was checking.",
 "case:hints.h_papers.levels.2": "In the Study, examine the desk diary and the letter tray.",
 "case:hints.h_poisoned.levels.0": "You know how he died now. Pin it down on the evidence board.",
 "case:hints.h_poisoned.levels.1": "Open the question ‘How did Lionel Thorne really die?’ on the board.",
 "case:hints.h_poisoned.levels.2": "Answer ‘Poisoned — cyanide in his whisky’, backed by Harrow’s cyanide statement (or the fern) and the polished whisky glass.",
 "case:hints.h_recording.levels.0": "Hobbs remembers Lionel’s exact words. Have you seen them written down anywhere?",
 "case:hints.h_recording.levels.1": "Lionel’s past letters and dictation reels are filed in Eleanor’s office. Compare them with what Hobbs heard.",
 "case:hints.h_recording.levels.2": "Answer ‘An old dictation reel playing on the tape recorder’ using Hobbs’s statement, the 15 November carbon copy, and the tape recorder (or the empty reel box).",
 "case:hints.h_study.levels.0": "Crime scenes are generous to those who look twice. Have you been over the study properly?",
 "case:hints.h_study.levels.1": "Lionel’s desk and its surroundings hold more than paperwork. Think about what he drank, and what he took.",
 "case:hints.h_study.levels.2": "In the Study, examine the whisky glass, the potted fern and the silver pill box.",
 "case:hints.h_switch.levels.0": "If the voice was a recording, how did it start at exactly the right moment?",
 "case:hints.h_switch.levels.1": "Look at how the recorder was plugged in, and ask Hobbs how the master’s lamp is normally set up. Then search the hall.",
 "case:hints.h_switch.levels.2": "Examine the telephone-table drawer in the Hall to find the time switch, then pair it with the unplugged desk lamp.",
 "case:hints.h_timeline.levels.0": "Every event of the evening is now on the record. Can you put them in order?",
 "case:hints.h_timeline.levels.1": "Open the timeline in your Notebook. Anchor the events whose times you know, then reason about the rest.",
 "case:hints.h_timeline.levels.2": "The true order: the quarrel, the ice, Finch’s call, Eleanor’s letters, the poison, bridge, the old reel, Daniel, Hobbs finds the body, Eleanor kneels.",
 "case:hints.h_tod.levels.0": "Lionel was a man of strict habits. Did he keep them all on Saturday night?",
 "case:hints.h_tod.levels.1": "Find out when Lionel was last seen alive, and when he took his heart tablet. Hobbs, Margaret and Dr. Harrow can help.",
 "case:hints.h_tod.levels.2": "Answer ‘Between 9.25 and 10.00 pm’ with Hobbs’s 9.25 statement, the pill box, and Harrow’s (or Margaret’s) statement about the ten o’clock tablet.",
